{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Abstract","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Abstract","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Derivative","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Analytic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.NormedSpace.Connected","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Growth","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Vanishing","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochSuslinComplex"],"declarations":84,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.eq_mul_of_fiveTermS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.eq_mul_of_fiveTermS","kind":"theorem","line":656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L656-L698","doc":"**Bloch–Suslin rigidity, conditional on a Dolbeault structure.** In the function class of\nany `DolbeaultStructure`, every Bloch-symmetric solution of the five-term relation on\n`ℂ ∖ {0,1}` is a real multiple of a fixed such solution `D` that is nonzero somewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.eq_zero_of_kS_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.eq_zero_of_kS_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":641,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L641-L654","doc":"A solution in the class with vanishing constant `k` vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":626,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L626-L639","doc":"`γ` is linear in the function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":617,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L617-L624","doc":"`ω` is linear in the function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.InClass.sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.InClass.sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":610,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L610-L615","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.InClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.InClass","kind":"def","line":606,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L606-L608","doc":"`φ` belongs to the class of `S` on `ℂ ∖ {0,1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.eq_zero_of_gammaS_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.eq_zero_of_gammaS_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":566,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L566-L602","doc":"**D3, abstract (closing).** If `γ` vanishes, then `φ ≡ 0` on `{0,1}ᶜ`. Both coordinates of\n`d φ` vanish (`∂̄φ = conj ∂φ` for real `φ`), so the `const` axiom makes `φ` constant, and\ninversion-oddness makes the constant `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":526,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L526-L564","doc":"**D3c, abstract.** If `γ` vanishes, then `ω ≡ 0` on `{0,1}ᶜ`. The function\n`F = z(1-z)ω` is holomorphic with the two symmetries and a growth bound; the class-free\ntheorem `eq_zero_of_symm_growth` (removable singularities and Liouville) kills it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_growth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_growth","kind":"theorem","line":453,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L453-L524","doc":"**D3a, abstract (growth at `0`).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.continuousAt_omegaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.continuousAt_omegaS","kind":"theorem","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L449-L451","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_holo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_holo","kind":"theorem","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L440-L447","doc":"**D2, abstract.** If `γ` vanishes on `{0,1}ᶜ`, then `ω` is holomorphic there. This is the\n`cauchyRiemann` axiom applied to `ω = ∂φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L422-L438","doc":"Reflection: `ω(1 - z) = ω(z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_inv","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L404-L420","doc":"Inversion: `ω(z⁻¹) = z² ω(z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_comp_of_eventuallyEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS_comp_of_eventuallyEq","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L387-L402","doc":"Differentiating `φ ∘ g = c • φ` near `z`, `g` holomorphic, gives `ω(g z)·g' = c·ω(z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS_normSq_eq_mul_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS_normSq_eq_mul_im","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L372-L382","doc":"**D1, abstract.** `Re γ · |z|²|1-z|² = k · Im z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.mixed_identityS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.mixed_identityS","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L305-L370","doc":"**D1b, abstract (mixed derivative).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS_ofReal_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS_ofReal_re","kind":"theorem","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L301-L303","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS_conj","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L286-L299","doc":"**`γ` is real.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.first_identityS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.first_identityS","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L229-L284","doc":"**D1a, abstract.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.gammaS","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L224-L225","doc":"Its antiholomorphic derivative `γ = ∂̄∂φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.omegaS","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L221-L222","doc":"The `∂`-form of a real function, `ω = ∂φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_four","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L212-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dz_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dz_five","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L203-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L189-L196","doc":"**Real structure.** For a real-valued member, `∂̄f = conj (∂f)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_mul_holo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_mul_holo","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L183-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_holo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_holo","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L180-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dzb_comp","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L176-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dz_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.dz_comp","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Abstract.lean#L172-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.d_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.DolbeaultStructure.d_sub","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.co